# Icon-point band (H2 + icon points)

When a section is **heading + optional intro + 3 or 5 parallel points with icons** (no per-item links):

Use `IconPointBand`. Do **not** use cards, `FivePointGrid` stacked lists, or `Timeline`.

For **4** unlinked points as a 2 × 2 text grid (left-aligned, not centered), use `IconPointGrid` instead.

## Layout

- **Desktop (`md+`):** one horizontal row, equal columns (`repeat(N, minmax(0,1fr))`)
- **Mobile:** single column, same item structure
- Each point: **icon on top**, then title, then description — **left-aligned**, top-aligned
- Tight gap between each point title and its description (`mb-0.5`) — do not reserve extra title height
- Icons share one horizontal line
- No card box, border, background, or shadow on a point
- No connecting line, no step numbers, no centered process rail — this is not a timeline

## Counts

| N | Component |
|---|---|
| 3 or 5 unlinked points | `IconPointBand` |
| 4 unlinked points (2 × 2 text) | `IconPointGrid` |
| 5 linked items | `ServiceDirectory` (rows, not a band) |
| 4 linked / boxed items | P-05 / P-07 cards — only if the previous section is not cards |
